Figure 6 demonstrates how Nano-11 enhances antigen targeting to immunopotentiating cells and improves antigen retention at the injection site. Panel A shows that ovalbumin-positive migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) in the draining lymph node exhibit the highest CD86 expression compared to other cell types. Panel B further characterizes OVA+ and OVA− MigDCs, indicating that OVA, when adjuvanted with Nano-11, is predominantly associated with CD11b+ DCs and monocyte-derived dendritic cells. Panel C illustrates that Nano-11 significantly prolongs the retention of Alexa Fluor 647-labeled OVA at the injection site over time compared to soluble OVA, similar to aluminum hydroxide.